WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.860
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.270
The Café's Ghost Stories.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.680
Miss Sasako,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.450
we're going to do that tonight.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:42.720
Huh?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.940
We're actually going to do it?

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.940
What's "that"?

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.960
You know, that summer standard.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.290
Standard <i>(teiban)</i>?

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.530
That would be a blackboard <i>(kokuban)</i>.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.460
That would be bread <i>(shokupan)</i>.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.430
Those would be swim shorts <i>(kaipan)</i>.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.390
Those would be stairs <i>(kaidan)</i>.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.850
You are correct!

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.350
Wha?

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.020
We're going to tell ghost 
stories <i>(kaidan)</i>.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.730
Huh?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.780
In Preparations

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.240
I think this is everyone.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.450
Is it okay if I go home?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:30.760
He said he likes scary 
stories, so I brought him.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.210
I said I don't like them!

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.260
Will this work for the candle?

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.290
Yes.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.350
That's unnecessary!

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.680
I knew it.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.370
I knew this would happen.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:51.270
I think it sets the mood.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.730
Welcome to Polar Bear's Café's 
night of ghost stories.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.050
I wanna go home.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.980
You may see a ghost on your way home.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.700
Why would you say something like that?!

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.390
All right, fine.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.940
I'll stay.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.370
Then let's begin.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.040
I'll start.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.820
This is something I 
personally experienced

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.510
at the Llama Corner at the zoo.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.900
The only one in the Llama 
Corner that night

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.630
was me, who was working overtime.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.480
I was eating grass as usual,

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.130
when I felt a faint presence.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.400
P-Presence?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.290
But the other llamas 
shouldn't be there.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.690
I thought it must be my imagination,

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.370
so I started eating the grass again.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:52.650
However, I still felt a presence.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.900
The presence kept coming closer,

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.330
and was finally right behind me.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.150
I spun around quickly

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.260
and saw something that 
shouldn't have been there...

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.040
A zebra.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.990
The zebra that shouldn't have been there

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:19.090
vanished without a 
trace right after.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.930
Oh. Was that not scary?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.700
It was a ghost zebra.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.770
Well, it's sort of hard to imagine 
a ghost zebra, I think...

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.900
Gives me chills just talking about it.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.670
A zebra!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.630
Zebra...

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.880
That's not scary at all.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.430
Okay, I'll go next.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.040
Panda?

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:57.750
You're asleep?!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.060
Panda!

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.330
Wow, you get sleepy when it's dark.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.540
Come on, now...

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.100
Okay.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.370
The other night,

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.450
when I was lying on my 
bed, trying to sleep...

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.420
Huh?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.830
What time did I fall asleep?

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.390
Who cares what time?

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.470
Continue.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.390
But I'm tired right now.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.710
Come on now, Panda.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.640
Okay.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.680
As I was sleeping on my bed,

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.860
there was a weird sound by my pillow.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.780
I wonder what a weird 
sound sounds like?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.150
You shouldn't be asking me.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:51.600
What kind of sound was it?

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.990
I forgot.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.520
That's enough, Panda.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.280
Why don't you just listen?

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.460
Okay!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.540
Then I'll go next!

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.130
It happened last summer...

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.370
Please stop!

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.220
But I haven't said anything yet.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.880
Your face is scary enough!

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.670
Then I'll... go...

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.100
Go for it, Tortoise.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.140
Tell us a really scary one.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.190
The... animal... loving...

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.100
Takashi...

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.160
Could you pick up the pace a bit?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.410
Okay...

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:43.380
Takashi... died...

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.340
His mother... would take...

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:55.310
the bread crust... 
that he... liked so much...

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:59.990
to his grave... every... day...

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.840
Let's jump ahead,

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.660
otherwise this isn't going to end.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:05.750
Okay.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:13.040
One day... there was a voice... 
coming from the grave...

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:17.160
<i>Mommy, I'm sick of 
bread crust </i>(pan no mimi)<i>.</i>

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:23.080
Takashi

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.800
<i>Then what would you like?</i>

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.080
<i>That would be...</i>

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:30.050
Your... ears <i>(mimi)</i>...

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.610
Huh?

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.940
You were... asleep?

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.390
You're a bit too slow.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.520
The timing is too slow to get scared.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.170
Ears!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.130
Ears!

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:53.320
You're really good at being scared, Mr. Handa.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.630
Okay then,

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.780
I'll go next.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:59.840
I will now tell you

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.840
a tale of a penguin

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.870
from a world unknown to you.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:09.390
It happened when this penguin 
went to a certain bakery.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.800
There was a pretty girl penguin
 who worked there.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:20.470
The penguin went there day after day,

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.400
just to see her.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.520
However,

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.820
what he thought
 was one girl penguin,

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.780
turned out to be seven!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.060
That must have been really scary.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.150
It was.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:44.250
But that's the wrong kind of scary.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.740
It's not ghosts that are 
scary, it's penguins.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.630
It must have been hard,

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:51.910
Mr. Penguin.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.690
It's hard.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.220
Every day.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:58.260
It just happens that I have a

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.180
scary and painful tale, too.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:01.470
What?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.140
Really?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.220
Yes.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.380
It goes...

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:13.580
Once upon a time, when my 
hair was still black...

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.450
Hold on a second!

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.010
What's with this story?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.320
You can't wait?

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:25.950
Yeah, but you're going to continue 
the story anyways, right?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.530
Yep.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:33.210
One day, after catching a lot of salmon at the river,

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:39.960
I had eaten my fill and was taking a nap,
 when I heard a noise right by my ear.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.770
It was the sound of a mouse biting my ear.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.190
In my overwhelming fear,

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.240
my fur turned white.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.960
And to this day, I am scared of mice—

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.000
Hold it.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.780
This story is scary for a 
completely different reason.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.220
Not good?

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:05.200
Not good!

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.550
What kind of reason?

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.460
You don't need to know.

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:12.420
M-M...

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:15.030
Mice... mice...

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.750
You're such a good customer, Mr. Handa.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.510
You're next, Miss Sasako.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.280
I'm not really good at this.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.480
I'm not very fond of scary stories.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:30.980
I-I'm the same way.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:36.440
But I would like to hear 
your story, Miss Sasako.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.020
All right. Just a short one.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.330
...As they turned around...

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:51.630
Stop!

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.340
That's too scary.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.300
That's enough!

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.740
But I was just getting 
to the scary part.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.890
I'm sorry, but you can stop now.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.560
Mr. Handa!

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.670
See you later, Mr. Handa!

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.610
If you see a ghost, give me a call!

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.100
Bye-bye!

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.980
<i>Maybe I should go home 
with someone tonight.</i>

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:26.590
Mr. Handa.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:33.380
Are you scared to go home 
by yourself, Mr. Handa?

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.370
Well...

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.620
In that case,

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.180
if you don't mind, I'll see you home.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.270
Um... Th-Then...

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.730
I see.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.750
I'm heading in the same 
direction as Mr. Handa,

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.990
so I can see him home.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.960
Um, but...

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.850
Don't worry about it.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.230
Well then, Mr. Llama, Mr. Handa.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:06.240
See you later.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:07.520
See you later.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.300
See you later...

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:21.760
Hey.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.130
Is this how this should have ended?

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.510
I think so.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.720
Since he gets to go home 
without being scared.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.570
Mr. Handa,

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:32.880
have you ever seen a ghost camel?

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.720
No, I haven't!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.350
I saw one in the bathroom 
the other day.

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:39.440
What?! You did?!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:49.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:54.870
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.320
Panda Runs Away from Home.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.840
Panda

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.590
Huh? Panda?

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:07.290
That's a lot of luggage. 
Are you running an errand?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.520
Please don't ask.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.030
See ya.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:22.580
And so,

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.400
I was like,

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:28.620
"Maybe it was a house demon."

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.510
More importantly,

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.450
how are things with Miss 
Penko and the others?

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:38.240
Could you let me forget about 
that as long as I'm here?

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:42.220
Right now, I just want to talk 
about the house demon.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.640
Running away from reality?

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.640
Call it what you want.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.320
I can't get in.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.190
What's with all the luggage?

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.720
Going to the flea market?

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.760
You seem down.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:01.030
Did something happen?

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.150
Mom is always getting mad at me.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:10.160
There you go, lazing around again.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.170
What's wrong with a 
panda lazing around?

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.370
Well, I guess they are 
usually lazing around.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:20.190
If you take lazing around from me,

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.350
there won't be anything left.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.090
So there won't be anything left?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.340
That's amazing in its own right.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:33.290
My mom must hate me.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.060
Um...

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.020
Maybe your mom wants 
you to help out more.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:43.770
But my little brothers and 
sister laze around, too,

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:46.040
and she doesn't get mad at them.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.510
Well,

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:50.030
it's probably because they're 
still really young.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.560
It's because my little brothers 
and sister are cute,

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:57.120
but I'm not.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:00.450
But all pandas are cute.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.590
This is a picture of my little sister.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.550
Wow.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.220
I guess there is a difference.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.050
Yeah.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:14.970
Oh.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:20.410
So I am a child that was 
found under the bridge.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.150
If you could actually find 
a panda under a bridge,

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.840
then all the zoos would 
have looked by now.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.070
So, what's wrong?

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.030
Actually, I ran away from home.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:34.420
Oh, I knew it.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:35.600
I see.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.520
So, where are you going to go?

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:38.450
Under the bridge?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.260
What?

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.260
Couldn't you worry a bit more

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:44.810
and invite me to your 
house or something?

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:45.900
Nope.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.010
So, where are you going?

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.030
Let's see,

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.970
a place where I can laze around 
without being yelled at,

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.660
somewhere I'll be fed 
without having to ask,

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:59.580
and somewhere there's 
someone to call me cute.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:03.560
That's limiting things 
quite a bit, isn't it?

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:04.400
Oh,

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.860
what about Rin Rin's?

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.820
Welcome Panda!

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.820
No!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.590
I want him to stay even further away.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.380
Then what about the zoo?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:19.290
You could live there while you work.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.210
Wow, Mr. Panda's so cute!

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:27.470
Why do I have to work every day?

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:32.170
I don't wanna work every day.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:35.800
I don't think that's something 
you want to say so boldly.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:36.680
Oh.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.220
What?

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:42.040
Could I leave my stuff 
here, Polar Bear?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:42.640
Huh?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.490
I'm gonna go eat dinner at home.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:47.650
See ya later!

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.390
He's going home...

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:54.140
Apparently there's many 
forms of running away.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.820
I don't think this is 
called running away.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.120
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.830
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.660
Panda still hasn't come 
by to pick up his luggage

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.520
from when he ran away?

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:14.340
Yeah, he hasn't been back since 
he went home for dinner.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.340
So he slept at home.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.480
Yep.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.740
Isn't there something wrong with 
this method of running away?

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:26.040
I came to continue my running away.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.820
You know, Panda,

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.660
if you go home when you're hungry,

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:36.300
it's not really running away.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:40.260
How do I put this... It's daily life.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.790
I'm not going back home.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.670
I'm not going back anymore.

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:48.080
Well, you can go back.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.920
What happened?

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.880
Something really shocking 
happened again last night.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:18:00.850
It's your birthday next week, 
but I'm a little busy.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:04.680
Born in September

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:02.760
So we'll celebrate next month,

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.500
along with your little siblings.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.420
Well, that makes it easier for your mom.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:12.370
I mean, then she'll only 
have to buy one cake.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.860
But you should be able 
to have multiple cakes.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.080
The more celebrations 
there are, the better.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:22.330
So why would she try to limit them?

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:26.220
Jeez, I can't stay there anymore.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:27.540
Now, now.

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:29.740
In that case,

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.850
why is she holding his birthday 
with the younger siblings'

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:36.260
instead of holding theirs with his?

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.300
Wow.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:42.990
Isn't she cute?

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:45.600
That's not right, Polar Bear.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.780
You can't compliment the 
picture of the cute sister,

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.330
in front of Panda who isn't cute.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.690
Whoops, sorry.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.070
Hold on a sec, Panda.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.900
They are giving you a celebration,

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.880
even though it's a month late.

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:04.190
I think you're going to 
have to compromise.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.360
I don't want to!

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:07.660
Why?

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:13.070
Because I wanted a panda snow 
cone maker as a present.

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:17.630
In a month, I won't want 
to eat snow cones anymore!

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.220
Really? That's the reason?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.910
I'm just going to be your 
child, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:28.100
Hey! Don't make yourself into my family!

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.980
So you don't think I'm cute, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.940
That's not the issue here.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.470
I think it'd be fine if you 
let him stay with you.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:43.150
Wha— Miss Sasako?!

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.610
What are you saying?!

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:50.020
Then I'll be a child at Miss 
Sasako's or Polar Bear's.

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.550
That's not going to happen.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:58.110
So no one wants me as their child.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:02.030
It's because I'm not cute.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.600
That's not the problem...

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.230
Oh.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:12.520
What if we give you a snow 
cone maker this month?

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:15.290
Let's have a snow cone party.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:21.400
Really?! When? When?

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.110
This is today.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.080
When? When?

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.080
The Café is closed on Sunday...

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.130
Oh, there's a meeting

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.670
with the neighborhood 
association next week.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.750
The week after that, I have a 
Buddhist memorial service.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:40.340
I'll be at a relative's wedding that week, too.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.430
Then...

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:45.430
Oh, that'll make it next month.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.490
W-What about this weekend?

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.740
Maybe Saturday afternoon?

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:52.620
Sure.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.510
Great idea!

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:57.610
Okay, see you.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:00.350
I'm going home.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.810
So you're done running away?

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:03.700
Yep.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.570
Why don't you take your 
luggage with you?

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.890
Oh, we're going to need it

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:11.040
if we're having a snow cone party.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.460
Ice

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:19.530
This is essential for snow cone parties.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.880
I really do think there's something wrong

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.430
with your method of running away.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:28.800
I can't wait for the weekend!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:32.810
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:35.270
Ice

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.250
It's rather cool today.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.920
Maybe we'll have to cancel 
the snow cone party.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:42.740
I think so.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:46.820
Oh.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.410
Let's do it! Let's do it right now!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.240
Yes!

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.840
Thank you for the meal!

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:07.300
You know,

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.000
it's not very good on rainy days.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.720
Yep.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:24.860
Polar Bear's Café

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:24.690
Next Time

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.500
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:00.580
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:04.160
We had your family gather here today.

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:05.510
Why did you have them come?

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.210
It's a little embarrassing.

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:10.760
Mr. Penguin, hurry up and 
start the family meeting.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:13.260
I think the subject should 
be Mr. Penguin's future.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:13.260
Emperor Penguin Chick

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:13.260
King Penguin Chick

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.550
That's not for everyone to watch.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:16.310
Let's end this.

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:18.140
Next week's Polar Bear Café

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:19.620
will be presented in double speed.

00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:21.390
You just try it.

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:22.140
Enjoy!

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:23.980
Sorry, you really didn't have to do it.

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.520
There Are Many Kinds of Penguins 
